{"base_rate":0.15269461077844312,"brier":0.07166182634730539,"bss":0.44610914570775306,"bss_hi":0.540848042805037,"bss_lo":0.3242063276839324,"chart":{"base":[260.0,52.5],"fp":[218.3,323.1],"lead":"62,273 272,255.9 482,251.3 692,226.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.45 — higher than 84% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end +10pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 84% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 4%; promised 69% → rained 60%"},"rel":"75.4,449 499.7,204.9"},"country":"NE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.032559880239520965,"ess":337.4807114686453,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Zinder</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Zinder rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (92%), believe about\n<b>75%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 668 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 3.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.45, ranked 34 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(12&ndash;91) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>460</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>92%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 4 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Zinder</b> <span class=\"muted\">Niger</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.45</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>12&ndash;91\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>668 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Zinder &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Zinder\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.646434782608694,379.62608695652176 108.22972972972973,298.3783783783784 221.75181818181818,172.4242424242424 383.68,28.70588235294116 383.68,71.52941176470591 221.75181818181818,255.15151515151513 108.22972972972973,357.4054054054054 58.646434782608694,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"326.4191616766467\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"326.4191616766467\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.646434782608694,374.8782608695652 108.22972972972973,322.97297297297297 221.75181818181818,216.54545454545456 383.68,109.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 460 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.646434782608694\" cy=\"374.8782608695652\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 14%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"108.22972972972973\" cy=\"322.97297297297297\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 46%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"221.75181818181818\" cy=\"216.54545454545456\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"383.68\" cy=\"109.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(15%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Zinder the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.47) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (0.06).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>148</td><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'>0.060</td><td class='num'>2.7%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'>0.239</td><td class='num'>9.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'>0.472</td><td class='num'>1.0%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>170</td><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'>nan</td><td class='num'>0.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":13.80716,"lon":8.9881,"n":668,"n_cities":213,"name":"Zinder","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.001826086956521739,"n":460,"obs":0.01956521739130435,"sig":true},{"hi":0.27600000000000025,"lo":0.06,"mean":0.14189189189189189,"n":74,"obs":0.16216216216216217,"sig":false},{"hi":0.75,"lo":0.27600000000000025,"mean":0.4625757575757576,"n":66,"obs":0.45454545454545453,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.75,"mean":0.92,"n":68,"obs":0.75,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.2,"provisional":false,"rank":34,"rank_hi":91.0,"rank_lo":12.0,"reliability":0.0032104981592204983,"resolution":0.05753524886142234,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"zinder","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Niamey"}